What is CPI?

The Consumer Price Index (CPI) tracks how prices change for everyday items like groceries, gas, and rent.

Formula:
\text{CPI} = \left( \frac{\text{Current Cost of Goods}}{\text{Base Year Cost}} \right) \times 100

CPI helps measure how fast your money is losing value due to inflation.

